13:56:52 said  I built **Sketchframe**, a sketch-style screen designer in Rust that runs on Mac, Windows and Linux. It has about 120 drag-and-drop parts in a hand-drawn look, with a clean look as an option. There are 15 device frames, including phones with a camera cut-out, Android, foldable and flip phones, tablets, round and square watches, laptops, monitors, browsers, TVs, car displays and VR windows. It also has a built-in AI connection (MCP): an assistant like Claude can create screens, place and link parts, and look at a picture of the result, and you see each change live and can undo it.
13:56:52 said  I decided the AI connection lets assistants both read and edit your screens, since that seemed closest to what you asked for. The Help menu has a window with the settings to copy into the assistant.
13:56:52 said  **Long-requested features I added:**
13:56:52 said  - Reusable components that update everywhere they're used.
13:56:52 said  - Template screens drawn underneath other screens.
13:56:52 said  - A layers list where you can hide and lock parts.
13:56:52 said  - Dark-mode screens and a dark app theme.
13:56:52 said  - Alignment guides, a grid and snapping.
13:56:52 said  - A clickable present mode.
13:56:52 said  - A flow map showing all screens and the links between them.
13:56:52 said  - Export to a clickable web prototype, PNG and SVG.
13:56:52 said  - Version history, screen notes and quick-add by typing.
13:56:52 said  **Tested:** the build passes the check, and I looked at pictures of the editor, present mode, the flow map, every device frame, and an AI-created watch screen.
13:56:52 said  **Not tested:**
13:56:52 said  - I didn't drag parts around by hand.
13:56:52 said  - I haven't run it on Windows or Linux.
13:56:52 said  - The hand-drawn lettering uses the computer's Comic Sans (or Comic Neue on Linux), so it looks plainer where neither is installed.
13:56:52 said  - Which features people asked for most over the years and how close the look is to the original are my best estimates, since I had no original or feature-request pages to compare against.
13:56:53 said  A good next step would be to tell me which three missing features matter most to you, or to try having an AI assistant design a full sign-up flow and see how the result feels.
